                <pb facs="0846" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg752"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure in No. 2429.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from the Register of Citizens of the United
                        States kept at this Consulate-General.</hi></head>
                <p>August, 1878. Julio Sanguily, 32 years of age; native of the Island of Cuba;
                    married; profession, commerce; transient, residence San Rafael Baths.</p>
                <p>Naturalized as a citizen of the United States on the 6th of August, 1878, by the
                    superior court of New York. Passport No. 9310 issued by the Department of State,
                    at Washington, on the 7th of August, 1878. Government-general of the Island of
                    Cuba issued him personal document (“cedula personal”), dated the 22d of August,
                    1878.</p>
                <p>I certify that the preceding is a faithful extract from the register kept in this
                    consulate-general.</p>
                <closer><signed>(Signed) <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramon O. Williams</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
